<!--
  The native unshield confirmation (spec 2026-11-08 shielded A0 M1 §4 step 3, I7). Read by the
  privacy-claims guard (src/screens/shielded/__tests__/privacyClaims.test.ts): no string here may
  claim a privacy property the scheme does not deliver. The values the dialog shows (owner, token
  account, amounts, pool) are Rust's; these are only the labels and the two sentence frames.
  %1$s / %2$s / %3$s are filled by A0ConfirmText.render (Locale.ROOT). The token's symbol (the
  amount line's %3$s, the fee line's %2$s) is Kotlin's own, chosen from BuildConfig.A0_NETWORK
  (devnet → TEST, otherwise NOC; M1c Task 8) — never a value from JS.
  Shielded UX part B (spec 2026-11-20 §2 row 9): the user-facing words are "making public" / "private balance"; src/copy/__tests__/nativeStrings.test.ts holds them equal to src/copy/modes.ts.
-->
